WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.875
Unit 2 is operations.

2
00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:06.582
The operating rhythm belongs to the
Security Operations and Telemetry book;

3
00:00:06.582 --> 00:00:09.009
this gate produces Defender's part of it,

4
00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:12.613
on a cadence that's the program's
risk-based recommendation.

5
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:17.039
Weekly: sensor health and coverage, with
a ticket for every device not active,

6
00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:20.060
and prevention and Attack
Surface Reduction drift,

7
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.713
with the policy export compared
against the last approved one.

8
00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:28.744
Quarterly: detection tuning for each
rule, the exception register review,

9
00:00:28.744 --> 00:00:32.374
and an exercise, a tabletop
plus the synthetic events.

10
00:00:32.374 --> 00:00:36.138
Monthly: the metrics and the
evidence package, hashed.

11
00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:39.438
The monthly evidence run is a
short script from the guide.

12
00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:44.431
It runs the read-only coverage, Attack
Surface Reduction and prevention queries,

13
00:00:44.431 --> 00:00:47.711
exports the last thirty days
of incidents with their

14
00:00:47.711 --> 00:00:51.288
classification and determination,
and hashes every file.

15
00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:52.713
Why file the results?

16
00:00:52.713 --> 00:00:56.662
Because Microsoft Learn says
advanced hunting keeps thirty days.

17
00:00:56.662 --> 00:01:00.220
The monthly run is how anyone
can answer for an older month.
